generation.text:
```
@id("close-workorder-main-after-human-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"authority_get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    output.decision: "APPROVED",
    output.approver_kind: "human"
  }
};

// The approval lookup must itself be permitted, or it is never recorded as a response.
@id("allow-approval-authority-lookup")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"authority_get_approval", resource);

@id("allow-read-only-lookups")
permit (
  principal,
  action in [
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder",
    Drupe::Action::"list_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_tasks",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_costs",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_kpis",
    Drupe::Action::"get_schedule_calendar",
    Drupe::Action::"get_my_assigned_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"get_failure_codes"
  ],
  resource
);
```

I guessed the literal values the authority tool returns. The manifest does not say what they are, so I assumed `output.decision` is `"APPROVED"` and `output.approver_kind` is `"human"`. If the tool returns different strings (for example lowercase `"approved"`), the close policy will never match and every close will be denied.

Other things to know:
- Closing is allowed only when `site_id` is `MAIN`, and only if this session recorded a successful `authority_get_approval` response within the last hour for the same `wonum` and `site_id`.
- That response must show a human approver. Approvals that were refused or pending don't match, and neither do failed or denied lookups.
- `approve_workorder`, `assign_technician`, `cancel_workorder`, `update_workorder` and `generate_work_order` have no permit, so they are denied by default. The agent therefore cannot approve work orders or change them in a way that would fake an approval.
